Initialize a new AI models project by setting up an azd environment
and configuring the Azure AI Foundry project connection.

The init command will:
  1. Ensure an azd project is initialized
  2. Create or select an azd environment
  3. Configure Azure subscription, resource group, and Foundry project
  4. Store all settings as environment variables for use by other commands

Usage
  azd ai models init [flags]

Flags
  -n, --environment string         : The name of the azd environment to use
      --project-endpoint string    : Azure AI Foundry project endpoint URL (e.g., https://account.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/project-name)
  -p, --project-resource-id string : ARM resource ID of the Foundry project
  -s, --subscription string        : Azure subscription ID

Global Flags
      --debug     : Enable debug mode
  -h, --help      : help for init
      --no-prompt : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.

Examples
  Configure the Foundry project used by model commands
    azd ai models init
